# func/text/tx_cp (id 324): unit copier with a filter, the shared engine of CLEAN, TRIM, PROPER,
# CONCAT(ENATE), TEXTJOIN, REPT, REPLACE and SUBSTITUTE. One source unit per step, appended to the
# output string being built (one write per emitted unit, ev_fmt_emit style), one read per 3 units.
# Registers: P0 next source word address, N0 = SK units to skip first, N1 units left to consume
# (skipped ones included), T0 mode (0 copy, 1 CLEAN, 2 TRIM, 3 PROPER), T2 SW current source word
# (consumed units shifted out), T3 SWN units left in SW, T4 WA output word address, T5 ACC output
# word being filled, T6 POS units in ACC (0..2), T7 LEN units emitted, T8 st filter state.
# PC 0: N1 <= 0 -> return (LR, LP). SWN = 0 -> read [P0], P0 += 1, PC 1. Else one unit.
# PC 1: SW = x0, SWN = 3, and one unit from it in the same step.
# Unit: skip (SK > 0): consume, SK -= 1. Else filter: copy emits; CLEAN emits units >= 32; TRIM drops
# spaces (U+0020) at the start and repeated ones, and holds one pending space (st 2) that is emitted
# only before the next non-space (that step emits the space and does not consume); PROPER upper-cases
# a letter after a non-letter and lower-cases a letter after a letter (st = previous was a letter).
# Emit: ACC += v 2^(16 POS), write ACC at WA; POS 2 -> WA += 1, ACC = 0, POS = 0. LEN += 1.
# Note: weights/func/text/tx_cp.md
